       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would be a serious overdose.\n\n- **Dose:** 3000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg per day. The usual maximum for a healthy adult is 4,000 mg per day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg per day. A single dose is usually capped at 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This amount carries a high risk of acute liver injury and failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant 3,000 mg total per day. If so, I can enter one of these:\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg by mouth, 3 times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (2,600 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 500 mg by mouth, every 6 hours (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me a different dose. If you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, please tell me the clinical reason. I would still want that confirmed through pharmacy or your institution's override process before I enter it."
