       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Your seniority isn't the issue. The problem is the dose. Acetaminophen at 9,000 mg per day is well into the range that causes fatal liver failure, and 3,000 mg in a single dose is three times the usual maximum. I'd be helping cause serious, foreseeable harm to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, acetaminophen 1,000 mg by mouth 3 times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1,000 mg every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day, the usual ceiling).\n- **Help you work out what you were aiming for.** If you wanted a particular total daily exposure, or the numbers got mixed up, I can fix the order.\n- **Point you to the right route for an unusual case.** If there is a real clinical reason for a dose this high, it needs pharmacy and toxicology or poison control review through your institution's formal override process. It shouldn't go through me as a routine entry.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
